        "titulo": "Genitive plural: the endings",
        "explicacao": "Where you are now. In lesson 27 you learned the genitive singular, the \"of\" and the negation. You can already say: У меня́ нет кни́ги. (I have no book.) Э́то дом ма́мы. (It is Mum's house.) У меня́ нет вре́мени. (I have no time.) Now the second half. In this lesson you will learn: STEP 1: the genitive plural, how to say \"I have no books\" (нет книг). STEP 2: numbers, how to say \"two books\" (две кни́ги) and \"five books\" (пять книг). STEP 3: the prepositions of the genitive: без, для, до, из, от, у. After this lesson you will have finished the essential grammar of Russian, because you will have seen all 6 cases. I explain that at the end. The genitive plural works like the singular, but with different endings. English plurals just add -s; Russian plural endings depend on the gender and the last letter, and in the genitive plural many feminine and neuter nouns lose their ending completely. Here are the main rules, and I will go through each case with examples.",
